From: Codex <codex@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] explorer: allow an external shell to own the shell window

Purpose: opt out of claiming GetShellWindow in the builtin desktop manager.
XP behavior: native explorer checks for an existing shell and delegates to it.
Observed: native XP explorer exits without creating Progman when Wine already
registered its desktop HWND. Keep Wine desktop management, yield shell identity.
Set WIN4WINE_EXTERNAL_SHELL=1 for native shell sessions only; unset for fallback.
Derived from Wine source and WINEDEBUG relay logs, without disassembly.

diff --git a/programs/explorer/desktop.c b/programs/explorer/desktop.c
index e0b57a4..3dbc053 100644
--- a/programs/explorer/desktop.c
+++ b/programs/explorer/desktop.c
@@ -1176,6 +1176,9 @@ static void set_shell_window( HWND hwnd )
     HDESK desk;
     WCHAR desk_name[MAX_PATH];
 
+    /* Keep desktop management alive while a native shell owns the shell HWND. */
+    if (GetEnvironmentVariableW( L"WIN4WINE_EXTERNAL_SHELL", NULL, 0 )) return;
+
     if (!(winsta = GetProcessWindowStation()) ||
         !GetUserObjectInformationW( winsta, UOI_FLAGS, &flags, sizeof(flags), NULL ) ||
         !(flags.dwFlags & WSF_VISIBLE))
